    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d407">

                <pb facs="0549" n="447" sameAs="frus:frus1908/pg447"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 13116/2.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Minister Furniss to the Secretary of
                    State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Port au
                                Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1908-04-09"><hi rendition="#italic">April 9,
                        1908</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 355.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose herewith copies
                    of the correspondence between this legation and the Haitian department of
                    foreign <pb facs="0550" n="448" xml:id="pg448"/> relations relative to certain
                    Haitian authorities refusing permission to Americans to land at Haitian
                    ports.</p>
                <p>It would seem from Secretary Borno’s reply that there will be no further
                    difficulty. However, I am not unmindful of the fact that I have several times
                    informally discussed this matter with the Haitian Government and have been
                    promised that there would be no further annoyance, yet there has been no
                    amelioration until now.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">H. W. Furniss.</hi></signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d407-a1.xml" xpointer="d407-a1"/>
